SUMMARY:Full Moon · Anzac Bridge from Bicentennial Park\, Glebe · Moon be
 tween the pylons
LOCATION:Bicentennial Park foreshore\, Glebe NSW 2037
GEO:-33.87326;151.17759
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-33.87326,151.17759
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: The full moon climbing between the two white pylons of An
 zac Bridge\, across Rozelle Bay. Moonrise is at sunset\, and the moon reac
 hes the pylon tops in blue hour.\nTarget: moon centred on the centre of th
 e span\, level with the pylon tops.\n\nWHEN (Sydney time)\nFriday 22 Janua
 ry 2027  (work day)\nFull moon: Fri 22 Jan 23:17. Moon 100% lit at the ali
 gnment.\nSunset 20:06 · civil twilight ends 20:34\nMoonrise 20:05 at azim
 uth 63° ENE (sea level horizon).\nALIGNMENT 20:52: moon altitude 7.7°\, 
 azimuth 56.4°.\nArrive by 20:07. The moon moves about one diameter every 
 2 to 3 minutes\, so shoot from 10 minutes before to 10 minutes after.\n\nM
 OON TRACK\n20:22  altitude  2.7°\, azimuth  60.7°\n20:27  altitude  3.5
 °\, azimuth  60.0°\n20:32  altitude  4.4°\, azimuth  59.3°\n20:37  alt
 itude  5.2°\, azimuth  58.6°\n20:42  altitude  6.1°\, azimuth  57.9°\n
 20:47  altitude  6.9°\, azimuth  57.2°\n20:52  altitude  7.7°\, azimuth
   56.4°  << alignment\n20:57  altitude  8.6°\, azimuth  55.7°\n21:02  a
 ltitude  9.4°\, azimuth  54.9°\n21:07  altitude 10.2°\, azimuth  54.2°
 \n\nCAMERA POSITION\nExact alignment pin: https://www.google.com/maps/sear
 ch/?api=1&query=-33.87326\,151.17759\nNamed spot: Bicentennial Park foresh
 ore\, Glebe NSW 2037 (50 m from the exact pin). https://www.google.com/map
 s/search/?api=1&query=-33.87283\,151.17743\nSubject pin (Anzac Bridge): ht
 tps://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-33.86899\,151.18533\nFrom t
 he exact pin\, Anzac Bridge is 858 m away on bearing 56.4°.\nFrom the nam
 ed spot it is on bearing 59.7°\, so there the moon passes 3.2° left of t
 he target. Walk toward the exact pin to close the gap.\nStraight line from
  Neutral Bay: about 6 km.\n\nTIDES (BOM prediction\, Sydney (Fort Denison)
 )\nFort Denison is in the same harbour\, so times are close for this spot.
 \nHigh water Fri 21:30  1.46 m\nAt the alignment (20:52): about 1.43 m and
  rising.\nPredictions exclude swell\, wind setup and wave run up. Check BO
 M coastal waters and swell forecasts on the day.\nSource table: https://ww
 w.bom.gov.au/ntc/IDO59001/IDO59001_2027_NSW_TP007.pdf\n\nFRAMING (Sony A1)
 \nAnzac Bridge spans about 8.0° tall from here. The moon is 0.52° wide\,
  about 8 m across at this distance.\nLandmark filling 60% of the frame hei
 ght: FE 70-200mm F2.8 GM OSS II at about 105 mm.\nMoon dominant: FE 200-60
 0mm at 600 mm puts the moon at 23% of frame height (34% in APS-C crop mode
 ).\nTripod\, OSS off on the tripod\, 2 s timer or remote\, shutter 1/125 s
  or faster at 600 mm.\nStart: ISO 200 to 400\, f/8\, expose for the moon. 
 Bracket 3 frames at 2 EV after sunset and blend.\n\nFIELD NOTES\n- Public 
 foreshore park. Jubilee Park light rail stop is close.\n- City light build
 s quickly after 21:00. Bracket for the moon and the sky separately.\n- Cal
 m water in Rozelle Bay gives a reflection of the bridge lights.\n\nVERIFY 
 BEFORE YOU GO\nTPE Web (camera pin\, subject pin\, alignment time): https:
 //app.photoephemeris.com/?ll=-33.87326\,151.17759&center=-33.87326\,151.17
 759&z=16&dt=2027-01-22T09%3A52%3A00.000Z&sll=-33.86899\,151.18533&fovb=56.
 4&fovhfov=19.75&fovvfov=13.28&fovd=858&fovo=l&fovov=1\nIn TPE\, set the se
 condary height to about 120 m above ground to check the geodetics line.\nP
 hotoPills: Planner > red pin on the camera pin\, black pin on the subject 
 > Find > Moon\, elevation 7.7° > confirm the date. Use the AR view on sit
 e.\nHeights are approximate. Fine tune by a few metres on the day.\n\nSOUR
 CES\nMoon phases: US Naval Observatory 2027 table (aa.usno.navy.mil).\nMoo
 n and sun positions: computed with Skyfield and JPL DE421\, with standard 
 refraction.\nCoordinates: OpenStreetMap. Ground heights: SRTM 30 m via Ope
 nTopoData.\nTide predictions: Bureau of Meteorology 2027 tide tables\, Cop
 yright Commonwealth of Australia 2026. Based on Bureau of Meteorology info
 rmation that has been modified. The Bureau does not necessarily support or
  endorse\, or have any connection with\, this product\, and gives no warra
 nty about the information. Full terms: page 4 of the source PDF.
