SUMMARY:Full Moon · Anzac Bridge from Bicentennial Park\, Glebe · Late sp
 ring moon between the pylons
LOCATION:Bicentennial Park foreshore\, Glebe NSW 2037
GEO:-33.87353;151.17783
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-33.87353,151.17783
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: The full moon rising between the pylons of Anzac Bridge a
 cross Rozelle Bay\, in late twilight.\nTarget: moon centred on the centre 
 of the span\, level with the pylon tops.\n\nWHEN (Sydney time)\nSunday 14 
 November 2027\nFull moon: Sun 14 Nov 14:25. Moon 100% lit at the alignment
 .\nSunset 19:34 · civil twilight ends 20:02\nMoonrise 19:56 at azimuth 61
 ° ENE (sea level horizon).\nALIGNMENT 20:45: moon altitude 7.7°\, azimut
 h 53.9°.\nArrive by 20:00. The moon moves about one diameter every 2 to 3
  minutes\, so shoot from 10 minutes before to 10 minutes after.\n\nMOON TR
 ACK\n20:15  altitude  2.9°\, azimuth  58.3°\n20:20  altitude  3.7°\, az
 imuth  57.6°\n20:25  altitude  4.5°\, azimuth  56.9°\n20:30  altitude  
 5.3°\, azimuth  56.1°\n20:35  altitude  6.1°\, azimuth  55.4°\n20:40  
 altitude  6.9°\, azimuth  54.6°\n20:45  altitude  7.7°\, azimuth  53.9
 °  << alignment\n20:50  altitude  8.5°\, azimuth  53.1°\n20:55  altitud
 e  9.3°\, azimuth  52.3°\n21:00  altitude 10.1°\, azimuth  51.5°\n\nCA
 MERA POSITION\nExact alignment pin: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?ap
 i=1&query=-33.87353\,151.17783\nNamed spot: Bicentennial Park foreshore\, 
 Glebe NSW 2037 (87 m from the exact pin). https://www.google.com/maps/sear
 ch/?api=1&query=-33.87283\,151.17743\nSubject pin (Anzac Bridge): https://
 www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-33.86899\,151.18533\nFrom the exa
 ct pin\, Anzac Bridge is 857 m away on bearing 53.9°.\nFrom the named spo
 t it is on bearing 59.7°\, so there the moon passes 5.8° left of the tar
 get. Walk toward the exact pin to close the gap.\nStraight line from Neutr
 al Bay: about 6 km.\n\nTIDES (BOM prediction\, Sydney (Fort Denison))\nFor
 t Denison is in the same harbour\, so times are close for this spot.\nHigh
  water Sun 21:20  1.42 m\nAt the alignment (20:45): about 1.40 m and risin
 g.\nPredictions exclude swell\, wind setup and wave run up. Check BOM coas
 tal waters and swell forecasts on the day.\nSource table: https://www.bom.
 gov.au/ntc/IDO59001/IDO59001_2027_NSW_TP007.pdf\n\nFRAMING (Sony A1)\nAnza
 c Bridge spans about 8.0° tall from here. The moon is 0.52° wide\, about
  8 m across at this distance.\nLandmark filling 60% of the frame height: F
 E 70-200mm F2.8 GM OSS II at about 105 mm.\nMoon dominant: FE 200-600mm at
  600 mm puts the moon at 23% of frame height (34% in APS-C crop mode).\nTr
 ipod\, OSS off on the tripod\, 2 s timer or remote\, shutter 1/125 s or fa
 ster at 600 mm.\nStart: ISO 200 to 400\, f/8\, expose for the moon. Bracke
 t 3 frames at 2 EV after sunset and blend.\n\nFIELD NOTES\n- Public foresh
 ore park. Jubilee Park light rail stop is close.\n- The moon climbs furthe
 r north than in January\, closer to the left pylon.\n- Sunday night. Easy 
 return home.\n\nVERIFY BEFORE YOU GO\nTPE Web (camera pin\, subject pin\, 
 alignment time): https://app.photoephemeris.com/?ll=-33.87353\,151.17783&c
 enter=-33.87353\,151.17783&z=16&dt=2027-11-14T09%3A45%3A00.000Z&sll=-33.86
 899\,151.18533&fovb=53.9&fovhfov=19.77&fovvfov=13.29&fovd=857&fovo=l&fovov
 =1\nIn TPE\, set the secondary height to about 120 m above ground to check
  the geodetics line.\nPhotoPills: Planner > red pin on the camera pin\, bl
 ack pin on the subject > Find > Moon\, elevation 7.7° > confirm the date.
  Use the AR view on site.\nHeights are approximate. Fine tune by a few met
 res on the day.\n\nSOURCES\nMoon phases: US Naval Observatory 2027 table (
